==English==
[[File:Nottingham Pride MMB A5.jpg|thumb|An adult female human ([[woman]])]]

===Etymology===
From Late {{inh|en|enm|humayne}}, {{m|enm|humain}}, from {{der|en|frm|humain}}, from {{der|en|fro|humain}}, {{m|fro|umain}}, from {{der|en|la|hūmānus|pos=a|g=m||of or belonging to a man, human, {{l|en|humane}}}}, from {{m|la|homo}}, with unclear ''ū''. Spelling {{m|en||human}} has been predominant since the early 18th century.<ref>Random House Dictionary, 2010</ref> Not etymologically related to {{m|en|man}}.

