===Noun===
[[Image:Human.svg|right|thumb|Rendition of the humans on the [[w:Pioneer plaque|Pioneer 10 plaque]].]]
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|human being}} {{lb|en|narrowly|biology}} The tallest, most abundant and most intelligent of the [[primates]]; ''[[Homo sapiens]]''.
#: {{syn|en|human being|man|Thesaurus:person}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Humans''' share common ancestors with other apes.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2013|month=May-June|author=[http://www.americanscientist.org/authors/detail/katie-l-burke Katie L. Burke]
|title=[http://www.americanscientist.org/issues/pub/2013/3/in-the-news-45 In the News]
|volume=101|issue=3|page=193|magazine=w:American Scientist
|passage=Bats host many high-profile viruses that can infect '''humans''', including severe acute respiratory syndrome and Ebola.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=Apr 18 2013|title=Rock Paper Cynic|genre=webcomic|passage=If I ever have to choose between a future where killer robots hunt '''humans''' or a future where bacon supplies have run out ... Let's just say you better start running.}}
## {{lb|en|fantasy|scifi|mythology}} A human as contrasted from superficially similar but typically more powerful [[humanoid]] creatures; a member of the [[human race]].
##* {{quote-book|en|date=Mar 29 1994|author=Bill Watterson|title=Calvin & Hobbes|passage=Greetings. I am Blor-Utar from Zimtok-5. I have come to subjugate the '''human''' race. Do not resist. Why '''humans'''? Because, in addition to their value as slave labor, they are also delicious and nutritious!}}
## {{lb|en|fantasy|scifi}} {{n-g|A term of address for any human, often implying the listener's species is their only noteworthy trait.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|url=https://www.buttersafe.com/category/comic/page/496/|author=Alex Culang, Raynato Castro|date=Dec 29 2011|title=Buttersafe|genre=webcomic|passage=Greetings, '''human'''! You have stumbled into the dimension of the Snow People.{{...}}Flesh plows clear the streets to make them safe to drive.{{...}}Does this shock you, '''human'''? Do the ways of our world open your eyes to the truths of your own?}}
# {{lb|en|broadly}} Any [[hominid]] of the genus ''[[Homo]]''.

